{"id": "striviaqa0069", "pool": "striviaqa", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1783403249, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "760971df1e172c7bf1d6bc3b4ee980bf878d27e27419c4254baabbe495a6c145", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "In Greek mythology, which virgin goddess of the hearth, home and cooking gave up her seat as one of the Twelve Olympians to tend to the sacred flame on Mount Olympus, for Dionysus?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/striviaqa0069.wav", "input_sha256": "ece97b07de142e6992e475bb0ed731127a0ad02b0a7cdcd2e71996be85e90a17", "input_samples": 154093, "input_s": 9.631, "n_real_chunks": 10, "score": 0.3486, "act": 1.0, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "In Greek mythology, the virgin god dess of the hearth, home and cooking who gave up her seat as one of the twelve Oly mpians to tend the sacred flame on Mount Ol ympus for Dionys us was Hestia. She was often seen as the gentle and modest figure of domestic life, representing stability and family values. By surrendering her place among the gods, she demonstrated her devotion to the divine order and to the worship of Dionys us, ensuring that his cult could continue uninter ruptedly. This act reflects her selfless nature and the importance she placed on harmony within both the household and the pantheon.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 10, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 37, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/striviaqa/audio/striviaqa0069_conservative_local.wav", "s